    A container cannot modprobe - it has no /lib/modules - so the module
    must already be live in the kernel the container shares.

--- 1. the credentials file ---
    The password goes in a file, not on the command line and not in
    /etc/fstab. Both alternatives are readable by any local user:
      * /etc/fstab is world-readable by design (mode 644)
      * command-line arguments are visible in /proc/<pid>/cmdline, i.e.
        in ps output, to every user on the system

    /etc/samba/task01.creds -> mode 600 root:root
[PASS] credentials file is mode 600 (owner-only)
    contents (password redacted for this transcript):
      username=smbuser
      password=<REDACTED>
      domain=WORKGROUP

--- 2. does a command-line password really leak into ps? ---
    Testing the claim rather than repeating it. A background process is
    started with a fake password as an argument, and ps is inspected.
    processes exposing the fake password in ps: 1
[PASS] confirmed: an argument-passed secret IS visible in ps to any user
